\f0\b \cf0 Key Network Architecture Notes:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls37\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 The Bad Network (Single Point of Failure):
\f1\b0 \'a0Daisy-chaining switches creates single points of failure. If one link or switch goes down, all connected devices lose connectivity, which is inefficient and risky for business operations. \
\ls37\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Two-Tier Architecture:
\f1\b0 \'a0Also known as the 'Collapsed Core' model, this design features an\'a0
\f0\b Access Layer
\f1\b0 \'a0(where devices connect) and a\'a0
\f0\b Distribution Layer
\f1\b0 \'a0(which handles routing and traffic distribution). It uses multi-layer (Layer 3) switches to handle both MAC and IP addresses. \
\ls37\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Three-Tier Architecture:
\f1\b0 \'a0Used for larger campuses, this model adds a\'a0
\f0\b Core Layer
\f1\b0 \'97a high-performance, high-reliability backbone designed to handle heavy traffic between multiple distribution switches.                                                                     
\f3\fs18 	\'95	
\f0\b\fs26 Redundancy:
\f1\b0 \'a0To improve reliability, it is advised to use multiple distribution switches and redundant links to ensure that the failure of one device does not collapse the entire network. \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Study Advice from the Video:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls38\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Analyze Real-World Designs:
\f1\b0 \'a0The speaker suggests auditing your own workplace network to identify whether it follows a two-tier, three-tier, or other design structure. \
\ls38\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Use Certified Resources:
\f1\b0 \'a0The video emphasizes the importance of using high-quality study materials, such as Boson's CCNA courseware and NetSim, to prepare for certification exams effectively. \
\ls38\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Join a Community:
\f1\b0 \'a0Engaging with peers in communities (like the Discord server mentioned) can provide additional support and help when learning complex networking concepts. \
\pard\pardeftab560\partightenfactor0

